             r"\emph{The audit of past tests} (28/09/2026; operator order: ``it is possible that we did some past test in um.py the wrong way, we need to investigate''): " + _tx6(_a6.get("n_families")) + r" families (read from the registry), each with an auditor and an adversarial verifier instructed to refute, plus a completeness critic; the registry is read by hash (\texttt{" + _tx6(_a6.get("registry_sha16_bytes")) + r"}): " + _tx6(_ac6.get("achados")) + r" findings (" + _tx6(_ac6.get("sustentados")) + r" sustained, " + _tx6(_ac6.get("parciais")) + r" partial, " + _tx6(_ac6.get("refutados")) + r" refuted, " + _tx6(_ac6.get("novos")) + r" new), " + _tx6(_as6.get("CRITICO")) + r" critical, " + _tx6(_as6.get("ALTO")) + r" high; no sealed number wrong by arithmetic --- the errors are of input, design, statistics and reading, and the correction goes beside. Among them, beside, in both languages: (E1) the gate's experimental step reads a single one-sided rite (V11) and shallow $\Lambda$CDM also passes --- \texttt{NATURE\_TEST\_COMPLETED} is not discrimination; (E4) the D1 tension (V3 $" + _d1s6 + r"\sigma$, read from the sealed verdict; DR2) is \emph{conditional on the map of $\Omega_m$ in $R$} \textsf{[INPUT]}, and the inputs to correct are DR1 without correlations, the Planck covariance (Chen, Huang \& Wang 2019) and the massive neutrino counted twice; (E5) the neutrino verdict ($2.95\sigma$ \textsf{[DECLARED --- report of 28/09]}) depends on which NuFIT 6.1 table (the paper's; the website's gives $3.02$--$3.22\sigma$ \textsf{[DECLARED --- report of 28/09, §5]}) and the 1 eV scale is a normalization; (E3) in the echoes, the $\sqrt\beta$ amplitude needs typing under v372, the fiducial spin is \textsf{[INPUT]} (GWECO-01, audit of 28/09) and the PE V2 ``power'' is $1/\sigma$; (E7) ``the primary evidence'' is a historical title --- the body already carries the reclassification; (E2) echoes and ringdown as above. Verdict: \texttt{" + _v6(_a6) + r"}. "
