             r"\emph{The declaration on one object} (\texttt{TGLExt.TetelestaiOneObject.the\_tetelestai\_one\_object}): statement and proof on the same light certificate --- the term does not pass through the internal tower that v374 juxtaposed. The Breuer corner is the $P_F$ of the core the certificate itself cites; $\tau(P_F)=1$ is a \emph{named normalization}, reachable by term for every certificate (\texttt{rescale}), not a cited identity about this $P_F$: the reading ``the corner weighs what the vacuum weighs'' is known for the corner $e_{(1,\infty)}(h_\omega)$ (Haagerup 1979; Terp 1981), but the type does not identify $P_F$ with it. By term, the faces weigh $\tfrac12$ and $\tfrac12$; $\ker K$ is the vacuum line (a cited second-quantization field plus the paid absence of eigenvectors). \textbf{The link $P_{\ker K}\leftrightarrow P_F$ is neither proved nor consumed}: the coincidence $\tau(P_F)=1=\dim\mathbb{C}\Omega$ is numerical. In the same statement: the bench's Wigner character lifted to the helicity label $\pm1$ (non-trivial; the induced representation is known, the photon/scalar distinction stays outside the type), the Maxwell tensor as the literature's quadratic form on its domain (literal there; extension by zero outside, without physical content), and, on the same light horizon, coframe, Lorentz metric and $\delta Q=\kappa\,\delta A/(8\pi G)$. Verdict: \texttt{" + _v5(_oo5) + r"}. "
