             r"\textbf{What the program said}: the v24 literal, which printed the canonical base marker as zero and sustained two sentences of the canonical-form document (``inhabitant absent'', ``term absent''). Both were true on their date and stay as a dated record; from this version the flag is \emph{measured}: %s. "
             r"\textbf{What remains open, and the erratum does not erase}: the \emph{canonical} representative (\texttt{canonicalFullTGLWitness}) is not constructed --- and that too is now measured, not declared ---; genuine type III$_1$ is not statable in today's mathlib and lives in the external ledger; the physical identification is H2. The base is necessary, not sufficient: inhabiting the rigid type without the modular realisation is not the TGL theorem. "
